-- **Repair-completion discipline (WQ-229, CODEX external review 2026-09-11 — Will-ruled 2026-09-17 via Decision Deck tap 22:04Z, record `PROME/proposals/2026-09-11_wq229-repair-completion-discipline-RULED.md`):** for any fix to a check, gate, instrument or tool, **write the ACCEPTANCE CONDITIONS before editing** — the properties the repair must hold, in the defect's own terms, never a restatement of the reported symptom ("include pending files" was too narrow; "every pending change in the intended closeout is visible, INCLUDING files already committed earlier · unrelated work is excluded · the agent's own instructions request the right comparison" is the condition set, and it *is* the test list). **Test the NEIGHBOURS, not just the reproduction** — **CONSIDER** all five categories, **ordinary · overlap · wrong owner · missing information · concurrent activity**, and write a one-line justified **N/A** for any that does not apply (contract + fixture rules: `PROME/tools/tests/README.md`; the miss that kept F1 open was an OVERLAP — a path both committed and pending). ⚠️ **Consider, not perform: requiring five mechanically on every small repair IS the paperwork reflex this rule exists to reduce** (external review refinement 2). **A completion note distinguishes four states and never merges them: IMPLEMENTED · TESTED · INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED · STILL UNRESOLVED** — passing the author's own tests establishes *implemented*, never *verified* (`finding_adoption_is_not_validation`) — and **PROME supplies that note UNPROMPTED; Will gives the instruction once, never per repair** (refinement 1). **A CONSEQUENTIAL repair** — one touching a gate, a shared contract, a Will-facing surface, or a defect that has already recurred — **goes to an independent reader BEFORE it is called fixed**, and that reader devises **at least one counterexample of its own** rather than re-running the author's suite. A small self-contained fix does not. ⚠️ **Prefer promoting or repairing an EXISTING control to adding a new one** — a repeated defect earns a reusable test and a mechanical guard, never another description of the pattern (the `.claude/` parity gate already existed, already ran, and was ADVISE; it fired and the drift shipped anyway).
-- **Spawn-closeout discipline (WQ-249, Will-ruled 2026-09-14 15:36 ET, verbatim *"Just get those agents closed out and we need to make that process standard"*; record `PROME/proposals/2026-09-14_spawn-closeout-discipline-RULED.md`):** **a spawn is not complete when the desk DELIVERS — it is complete when the desk has been ASKED to close out and PROME holds the answer, or has RECORDED that it went dark before the ask.** **PROME owns this, never the desk:** an idle desk cannot know the terminal is about to close, so a desk going dark unasked is an ORCHESTRATION failure. At PROME's closeout, enumerate every desk with a TOUCH-class `PROME/state/ORCH_LOG.tsv` row dated today — **from the record, never from memory of the session** — and doorbell each live one **before PROME's closeout commit**. ⛔ **The check is on the ASK, never on detecting a closeout: PROME does not classify another desk's commits as "a closeout" by subject text** (`[[finding_status_token_membership_test_desupervises_improved_rows]]` — RED wrote *"closeout"*, HOMER *"closeout nudge"*, and a desk that described it better would read as a miss). **Four states, reported separately and never merged: ASKED→receipt · ASKED→still working · ALREADY CLOSED OUT (still enumerated, never silently dropped) · WENT DARK BEFORE THE ASK (named — the state the rule exists to make visible).** ⛔ Scope is PROME's own spawns/re-pings, NOT a session Will launched himself (WALTER 9/14 was Will's, and claiming it would be `[[finding_grading_a_disposition_on_a_book_you_do_not_own]]`). 🔑 **Why a disk check cannot replace this:** on 9/14 PROME's own `ORCH_LOG` CLOSE row recorded a genuine PASS — *"all idle with last delivery committed and zero desk-dir residue"* — and **a desk that is idle with everything committed and no residue is INDISTINGUISHABLE ON DISK from one that has closed out.** The difference lives only in the live pane, has no artifact, and its loss leaves no absence to detect afterwards. Mechanization is DOCKET L378 with its acceptance conditions written first (WQ-229).
